### Public API (consume these names exactly — CRITICAL for tasks 6/7/8/9)
- `ControlStateConfig` fields: `Parameters mtypes.ControlV2Parameters`, `PeerAliveTimeout time.Duration`, `UsePSKForInterEdge bool`, `Graph *graphpath.IG`, `Now func() time.Time`, `Publish func(mtypes.ControlV2Event)`.
- `NewControlState(ControlStateConfig) *ControlState` — Now defaults to `time.Now` when nil.
- `(s *ControlState).Register(ctx, mtypes.ControlV2RegisterRequest, controlPSKey string) (mtypes.ControlV2Snapshot, error)` — returns the registering Edge's own snapshot (self-peer filtered out); increments revision only on observable state change; emits `peer_change` after lock release; rejected NodeID returns `*ControlV2Error` via `req.Validate()`.
- `(s *ControlState).Report(ctx, mtypes.ControlV2ReportRequest) error` — heartbeats / candidates / pongs; unknown NodeID → `ErrControlStateUnknownPeer`; identical report leaves revision unchanged; pushes latencies into `Graph` when provided; emits `peer_change` after lock release.
- `(s *ControlState).SnapshotFor(nodeID mtypes.Vertex) mtypes.ControlV2Snapshot` — peer-safe view: requester's own record excluded, peer `PSKey` cleared, slices/maps deep-copied, requester's `LastSeen` and revision match the service state.
- `(s *ControlState).ControlKeyFor(nodeID mtypes.Vertex) (string, bool)` — for task 6 HMAC verifier; never exposes key through snapshot/JSON.
- `(s *ControlState).Revision() uint64` — monotonic; bump only on observable change.
- `(s *ControlState).SweepTimeouts() int` — removes peers past `PeerAliveTimeout`, bumps revision once if any peer removed; emits `peer_gone` per removed peer after lock release.
- Emitted event shape: `mtypes.ControlV2Event{Type: ControlV2EventPeerChange|ControlV2EventPeerGone, Revision, Data: mtypes.ControlV2PeerChangePayload{NodeID, NodeName}}` — task 7 event hub receives these via the configured `Publish` hook.
- Sentinel: `ErrControlStateUnknownPeer` for `Report` of an unregistered NodeID.

### Concurrency contract
- Single `sync.RWMutex` guards the entire peer map; maps are never iterated under a read lock during mutation.
- Snapshot construction runs under the write lock (Register) or read lock (SnapshotFor); the returned slice/maps are deep copies so callers can use them without re-locking.
- `Publish` is invoked OUTSIDE locks; if it panics the service is unaffected (no lock held at call site).
- `Graph.UpdateLatencyMulti` is invoked while the write lock is held; the graph is internally concurrency-safe and does not call back into the service.

